---@field metadata? gcp.unstable.serviceusage_v1beta1.DocumentMap Service-specific metadata associated with the operation. It typically contains progress information and common metadata such as create time. Some services might not provide such metadata. Any method that returns a long-running operation should document the metadata type, if any.
---@field error? gcp.unstable.serviceusage_v1beta1.Status The error result of the operation in case of failure or cancellation.
---@field response? gcp.unstable.serviceusage_v1beta1.DocumentMap The normal, successful response of the operation. If the original method returns no data on success, such as `Delete`, the response is `google.protobuf.Empty`. If the original method is standard `Get`/`Create`/`Update`, the response should be the resource. For other methods, the response should have the type `XxxResponse`, where `Xxx` is the original method name. For example, if the original method name is `TakeSnapshot()`, the inferred response type is `TakeSnapshotResponse`.

---@alias gcp.unstable.serviceusage_v1beta1.OperationList gcp.unstable.serviceusage_v1beta1.Operation[]

